[Music]  my name is Robin sued Fisher and I'm the  founder and chief ice-cream maker at  smitten ice-cream started off actually  at the GSB when I drove into  entrepreneurship and took a bunch of  classes in that space and decided to  focus on something I loved and was  passionate about and that was ice cream  my goal was to take a product I love and  make it even better looked into the  science behind ice cream and figured out  that a lot of the quality of the product  is a result of ice crystal formation the  colder you freeze a product the smaller  the ice crystals can be and the smaller  the ice crystals the smoother the  texture can be so if I could actually  freeze it really really cold I could  make it to order I started playing  around with liquid nitrogen which is  negative 321 degrees Fahrenheit and I  started literally at GSB I was sourcing  a tank of liquid nitrogen and making ice  cream in my backyard and pretty much by  the end of my two years there I was  known as the ice cream girl some people  didn't even know my name I was just the  ice cream girl actually spent the next  two years after the GSB working in a  basement shop with a brilliant engineer  and really just making ice cream over  and over again with different types of  mixing devices and we ended up with a  prototype of our now machine that we use  in our shop which we call burr what I  decided to do was just sort of go rogue  a little bit and figured I need  something to carry this you know forty  pound stainless steel device and a tank  of liquid nitrogen and I also wanted  something to sort of prove that I was  trying to do a wholesome approach to ice  cream despite that it looks kind of  modern so the Radio Flyer wagon idea  sort of came about  I was telling someone that I was selling  on the street and they're like Oh Wall  Street and I was like I have the the  street as in B Street and so that was my  life for the next nine months I just  sold ice cream on streets and alleys and  parks in San Francisco actually got to a  point where I was totally fine with it  not working I just wanted to know and  then we started getting lines and lines  of mines and selling out every day so we  were able to create enough momentum to  open up our first shop in Hayes Valley  San Francisco and that shop has now been  open for two years it's a very very  interesting shop and not it's actually  built out of a 40-foot long recycled  shipping container and what we did is we  cut that shipping container in half and  half is our tiny little kitchen and half  is our open retail front bar and on that  front bar you will see four of our bure  machines you can interact and watch your  very own ice cream being made right in  front of you  [Music]  actually get to see this fog it's a  legend in vapour that forms around them  scenes San Francisco fog over the  machine it has a double helical mixer  which together sort of scrapes every  surface of itself to create the  exceptionally small ice crystal and then  it has dietary software that controls  viscosity inducing so it it actually  gives real-time feedback and the machine  is quote smart and it knows when it's  created the perfect scoop and it stops  for you I think it's really hard to do  two things better than anyone else in  the world so we don't we just focus on  that one thing and we make sure that  everything that comes out of our shop is  that one thing done as best as possible  having such a small menu allows us to  pick the best of the best ingredients  and make sure that every single flavor  is his perfect as we can make it  it was delicious so we got the salted  caramel and it was very cold was what  Emily said about it she remarked how  cold it was but it was very smooth when  I eat their ice cream it tastes very  natural you could see like where it's  coming from they are full disclosure  around like the ingredients which is  always nice  I'd been in the consulting world and had  done a lot of biotech and healthcare and  large scale big companies and I really  wanted to go after something that was  more personable and actually got a real  human reaction from people ice cream was  always a thing for me and my family that  brought people together and was always a  thing that was a delightful moment in  the day  my advice for entrepreneurs is go after  something that you love and not just a  business idea I didn't have you know any  real success until you're four and so I  definitely don't think I could have kept  going unless I really loved what I was  doing  I've got about ten different hats that I  get to wear but it all comes down to  making people happy I definitely make  sure that part of my day is just seeing  the smiles in the faces of the customers  who come through the door it's me very  grateful to be to be where I am and for  the the path that I've taken  [Music]

